<title>UK: Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs up two at 61 in week.</title>
<headline>Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs up two at 61 in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of active oil and gas rigs operating offshore Northwest Europe totalled 61 in the week ending July 2, up two from the previous week, consultants Arthur Andersen said.</p>
<p>There were 30 rigs operating in British waters, unchanged from the previous week. The Norwegian sector was up two at 17. The Netherlands and Denmark were steady at 10 and three rigs respectively while Ireland had one rig drilling in its sector.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7629</p>
